@* The mark on the link back to the head of a long table: an arrow pointing up, which is the whole
   of what it has to say.

   Built to the same box, stroke and linecap as <see cref="SectionMark"/>, <see cref="JsonMark"/>
   and <see cref="RefreshMark"/>, so a control carrying this and a row carrying one of those are
   drawn at one weight. Hidden from screen readers: the link around it is named, and read out this
   would be the same thing twice. *@
<svg class="glyph" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"
     fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"
     stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
    @* The shaft, and the head at the end it runs out at. *@
    <path d="M10 16.4V4.6"/>
    <path d="M5.2 9.4 10 4.6l4.8 4.8"/>
</svg>
